# ANALOG: the STEPS page's steps as an analog sequencer: SEQ switches the views; the white keys switch steps
# on and off; K1-K4 the pitch faders of four steps, SELECT which four (then the pages either side); a step
# held and a knob turned: its GATE (velocity); OCT: the 16-step pages
wait 300
settp 1 LENGTH 32
tap SEQ
wait 150
expect page STEPS
tap SEQ
wait 150
expect page ANALOG
shot analog0.png
tapkey 0
wait 100
expect stepnote 1 1 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
wait 100
expect stepnote 1 1 65
turn K4 -1
wait 60
turn K4 -1
wait 60
turn K4 -1
wait 60
wait 100
tapkey 6
wait 100
expect stepnote 1 4 57
# the second four: steps 5-8
turn SELECT 1
wait 100
expect page ANALOG
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
wait 100
tapkey 7
wait 100
expect stepnote 1 5 67
# step 1 held, a knob: its GATE; let go: still on (no tap)
key 0 down
wait 50
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
turn K3 -1
wait 60
wait 100
shot analog1.png
key 0 up
wait 100
expect stepnote 1 1 65
expect stepvel 1 1 90
# past the fourth four: the page after; back: the fourth four
turn SELECT 2
wait 100
expect page ANALOG
turn SELECT 1
wait 100
expect page TEMPO
turn SELECT -1
wait 100
expect page ANALOG
turn K1 1
wait 60
turn K1 1
wait 60
wait 100
tapkey 21
wait 100
expect stepnote 1 13 62
# OCT+: steps 17-32
tap OCT+
wait 100
turn SELECT -3
wait 100
turn K1 1
wait 60
wait 100
tapkey 0
wait 100
expect stepnote 1 17 61
tap PLAY
wait 600
shot analog2.png
tap PLAY
# SEQ: back to STEPS
tap SEQ
wait 150
expect page STEPS
